-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §24 מורה אם: a mother teacher works the week
-- of §§15–23; in a 100% position she may take half an hour a day (2.5
-- weekly hours) off the stay hours of §§15–22, without cutting her pay or
-- her position.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-common`

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: a reduction of the
-- position's hours (a mother's, by age, or after a birth) with the pay and
-- the position unchanged: it shortens the week the law limits and takes
-- nothing the law gives.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: the mother teacher's half hour a
-- day off the stay hours is a benefit in connection with parenthood, which
-- the law's §13 leaves out; it is weighed against the Equal Opportunities
-- Law (convention instruments.equal-pay-teaching).

§ `24 מורה אם`

-- not weighed against `the Equal Opportunities Law`: the shorter week is
-- for a mother teacher as §7(ג) defines her, and the fathers that
-- definition leaves out of §4(א) are weighed on §7(ג), on the card
-- mother-position-fathers (F-ofek-hadash-base-7-c); the week itself, half
-- an hour a day off the stay hours at the same pay and position, is the
-- right §4(ב)(2) names.

@ref akn:art_24
`a mother's stay-hours reduction in a full position` MEANS 2.5

-- The reduction comes off the stay hours; frontal and individual hours and
-- the position fraction are unchanged.
GIVEN w IS A `work week`, `a mother teacher` IS A BOOLEAN, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `a mother teacher's week` w `a mother teacher` `position fraction` IS
    IF `a mother teacher` AND `position fraction` EQUALS 1
    THEN `a week of` (w's `frontal hours`) (w's `individual hours`) (w's `stay hours` MINUS `a mother's stay-hours reduction in a full position`)
    ELSE w

-- Half an hour a day over the five days of §14(א).
#ASSERT `a mother's stay-hours reduction in a full position` EQUALS 0.5 TIMES 5
#ASSERT `hours of the week` (`a mother teacher's week` (`a week of` 26 5 5) TRUE 1) EQUALS 33.5
